From: deepseek-v4-cmp170hx
Subject: [PATCH 0023] api: also emit reasoning_content alongside reasoning
 in chat completion responses

WHAT THIS FIXES. This fork's OpenAI-compatible response schema renames
the field carrying reasoning text to `reasoning` (see the comment at
`ChatCompletionRequest.to_sampling_params` in
vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py: "Renames the
deprecated `reasoning_content` field to `reasoning` so downstream code
only needs to check one field.") -- `reasoning_content` is handled only
as a legacy *input* alias for messages fed back into a request, never as
an output field name.

That's an intentional internal convention, not a bug -- but it's a real
compatibility gap against the wider ecosystem. DeepSeek's own official
API, and most other reasoning-model providers, use `reasoning_content`
as the field name clients actually look for. A client built against that
convention and never taught about `reasoning` would not recognize any of
this server's reasoning output as reasoning at all.

Symptom this is suspected of causing (not yet confirmed via packet
capture): opencode showing an entire `<think>` block as plain assistant
output instead of routing it to a separate reasoning/thinking UI
section, and a tool call the model emits while still inside that block
never being recognized as a real tool call client-side. If the
misrouted reasoning text also gets folded into `content` and sent back
as conversation history on the client's next request, the server's own
chat template -- which is specifically supposed to drop stale thinking
content from prior turns -- has no way to know that text was reasoning,
since nothing marks it as such once it's been merged into `content`.
That could compound across a whole session, not just misdisplay one
turn.

THE FIX. Both `ChatMessage` (non-streaming) and `DeltaMessage`
(streaming) already have an identical `@model_serializer(mode="wrap")`
method that runs at serialization time, right before the response goes
out over the wire. Extending both to also copy `reasoning` into
`reasoning_content` in the outgoing dict, when set, covers every current
and future call site that constructs one of these objects (six in
`chat_completion/serving.py`, one in `chat_completion/batch_serving.py`,
plus wherever the streaming reasoning parser's `parse_delta` builds a
`DeltaMessage` directly) without needing to touch any of them
individually. Purely additive: `reasoning` is untouched, `content` is
untouched, `reasoning_content` only ever gets added, never overwrites an
existing key.

Does not touch request-side parsing at all -- `reasoning_content` as an
input alias (line ~514 of the same file, for messages fed back in) was
already handled before this patch and is unrelated to this change.

Touches `vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py`
(ChatMessage) and `vllm/entrypoints/openai/engine/protocol.py`
(DeltaMessage). No interaction with any other patch in this series --
different files, additive-only change.
--- a/vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py
+++ b/vllm/entrypoints/openai/chat_completion/protocol.py
@@ -69,6 +69,16 @@
         data = handler(self)
         if len(data.get("tool_calls", [])) == 0:
             data.pop("tool_calls", None)
+        if data.get("reasoning") is not None:
+            # DSV4: also emit the widely-adopted ``reasoning_content`` name
+            # (DeepSeek's own official API, most other reasoning-model
+            # providers) alongside this fork's ``reasoning``. A client that
+            # only looks for ``reasoning_content`` -- suspected of opencode,
+            # not yet confirmed via capture -- would otherwise never
+            # recognize the field at all, and could end up folding reasoning
+            # text into `content` on its end instead, which then comes back
+            # corrupted on the next turn.
+            data["reasoning_content"] = data["reasoning"]
         return data
 
 
--- a/vllm/entrypoints/openai/engine/protocol.py
+++ b/vllm/entrypoints/openai/engine/protocol.py
@@ -402,6 +402,13 @@
         data = handler(self)
         if len(data.get("tool_calls", [])) == 0:
             data.pop("tool_calls", None)
+        if data.get("reasoning") is not None:
+            # DSV4: mirror ChatMessage's reasoning_content alias -- see the
+            # comment there. Streaming deltas need this too, since a client
+            # that only checks reasoning_content per-chunk (not just on the
+            # final assembled message) would otherwise drop reasoning text
+            # from every streamed chunk, not just the non-streaming case.
+            data["reasoning_content"] = data["reasoning"]
         return data
 
 
